--- SURFACE NOTES: SettingField (parity port of web/src/features/settings/components/SettingField.tsx) ---
- The web component is a pure presentational field wrapper: it renders a label row -- an uppercase, muted,
  wide-tracked <label> plus an optional inline <HelpIcon> (web/src/components/ui/HelpIcon.tsx) -- and then the
  field control passed as children. It performs no fetching. The only conditional render is the help affordance:
  it appears iff a help descriptor is supplied AND its resolved text is non-empty (the web
  `{help && <HelpIcon>}` gate together with HelpIcon's own `if (!text) return null`).
- Files:
    feature-views/SettingField.Model.cs  -- WinUI-free: SettingFieldHelp (web SettingFieldHelp i18nKey/content/for),
        SettingFieldModel (label + optional help), SettingFieldDisplay, SettingFieldProjection (the label
        upper-casing + HelpIcon's text/aria-label resolution), SettingFieldDiagnostics, SettingFieldRegistration.
    feature-views/SettingField.cs        -- WinUI 3 view (ContentControl): a column of [label row, field]. The label
        is a tokenized TextBlock (TsTypeLabelFontSize / FontWeights.Medium / DisplayTokens.TextMuted /
        tracking-wider) shown upper-cased; the optional help affordance is the shared TsHelpTooltip. The
        caller-owned field (the web children) is exposed via the Field property.
    TeslaSync.App.Tests/FeatureViews/SettingFieldTests.cs -- 20 headless tests (label passthrough + uppercase,
        help-text resolution incl. i18n-key-over-content + content fallback + empty-text suppression + whitespace
        truthiness, the affordance accessible name "Help for {id}" / "More info" incl. a localized template,
        diagnostics PII-safety, registration, null-arg validation).
- States: the web source is pure presentational and has NO fetch lifecycle, so the generic loading / error /
  stale / offline branches do not exist on this surface (same precedent as the sibling presentational leaves
  HighlightCard / AdvancedSettings). The reproduced branches are exactly the source's conditional renders:
  the label is always shown, and the help affordance is shown only when help resolves to non-empty text. Both
  real branches are reproduced and unit-tested; nothing is hidden behind a blank box.
- Shared components only: TsHelpTooltip (the inline help affordance, the @/components/ui counterpart of the web
  HelpIcon), DisplayTokens/TypographyTokens (P1/S9 tokens). No raw library imports, no inline styles, no
  hardcoded English in the view.
- i18n (all via the P1/S10 ILocalizer facade; English fallbacks = the web fallback strings; the keys the composed
  HelpIcon uses are already present in Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw):
    a11y.helpFor            = "Help for {0}"   (the per-field affordance label)
    help.tooltip.iconLabel  = "More info"      (the generic affordance label)
  SettingField itself is anonymous -- its label and help text come from the parent settings page, exactly as the
  web component takes them as props -- so it extracts no additional literal keys.
- Accessibility: the label is displayed upper-cased (web `uppercase`) but exposes its natural casing to Narrator;
  the help affordance (the only interactive element) carries the web aria-label as its Narrator name and the help
  text as its spoken description + visual tooltip. System font scale + reduced-motion are inherited from the
  shared primitives.
- Telemetry (P1/S11): view.opened slug=SettingField, PII-safe (never the label or help text), emitted once on Loaded.
- Repo hygiene (pre-existing integration-merge corruption that blocked the shared test build at this worktree HEAD;
  git-verified unmodified vs HEAD before repair; the fix restores the single-root state the file's own INVARIANT
  doc comments document):
